{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>גדלים</b> — twice here, and the other גדלים is the work of chains. And this is what they said in the Gemara: 'make gedilim' — for two גדלים are written, and twist it from within itself, as written: the work of chains, in the manner that chains are made." "<b>אשר תכסה</b> — in gematria, to include a blind person's garment, that he is obligated." "<b>אשר תכסה בה כי יקח</b> — a hint to what is stated in Nedarim: Rabbi Elazar exposes a handbreadth and covers a handbreadth at the time of relations. Another interpretation: אשר תכסה כי יקח — a hint to a Torah scholar who darkens himself in his tallit. Another interpretation: a hint — כי יקח אשר תכסה teaches that he is covered for all his sins."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:20.507199245Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}